            "source": "scripts/release/autopilot.sh:513-514 at 49ff6df5b8",
            "excerpt": "    MODEL_LADDER_CRUX_DIR=\"$AP/models-t1\" CRUX_CERT=\"$WT/evidence/crux/$V/prompt-certification.json\" \\\n      bash scripts/cascade-drain.sh --target \"$V\" --passes 30 > \"$AP/cascade.log\" 2>&1; rc=$?",
            "excerpt_sha256": "7f2963cc4131512cc5e9099bd4cbb035f027dd9be9d26055e829bd02ba296bcd",
            "failure_scenario": "none: if the values drifted from step 5, R7 in the cascade preflight would judge different receipts than the tagging step did.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "structural-row-line-continuation-unset",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The structural row scans the drain and cascade-publish.sh line by line with an awk regex requiring unset/export/declare and the variable name on the same line. An unset whose variable name sits on a continuation line is therefore not flagged. The earlier advisory probe read rc 0; this review confirmed it by reading the regex (lines 154-156), not by re-running a probe. Fails closed in effect: it needs a deliberate edit to the drain, which the 40 mutants and a reviewer both see."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_draft_gated.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 154
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Read of the per-line awk pattern; awk sees one record per physical line, so a backslash-newline split hides the name from the same-line match.",
            "failure_scenario": "A later edit writing `unset \\` then `CRUX_CERT` on the next line would strip the receipts from the cascade preflight while the structural row stays green; R7 would then refuse after the tag is public.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "structural-row-exec-c-bash",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The env -i / env - detector does not match `exec -c bash \"$0\" \"$@\"`, which also clears the environment. The earlier advisory probe read rc 0; this review confirmed it by reading the pattern, not by re-running it."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_draft_gated.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 150
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "The pattern lists env -i and env - only; exec -c is a third spelling of an empty environment.",
            "failure_scenario": "A cascade-publish.sh that re-execs itself with exec -c would drop MODEL_LADDER_CRUX_DIR and CRUX_CERT and pass the structural row.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
